IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-art-13: Article 13 (transparency and provision of information to deployers) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. The Omnibus did not change Article 13.
-- Every function takes the date asked, the AI system and the harmonisation facts and answers through the gate of P2-section-2-gate.l4: NOTHING when Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not apply to the system on the date asked,
-- JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) cuts the Article off, NOTHING where Article 2(13) says it may be limited. Reading a result: JUST TRUE the requirement is met; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered.
-- Qualifiers inside a limb ("where applicable", "when appropriate", "where relevant", "if any") are folded into the one yes or no of that limb: answer yes where the qualifier makes the limb inapplicable (fork F-qualifier-fold).

§ `Article 13(1): transparent operation`

-- src:332 | High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed in such a way as to ensure that their operation is sufficiently transparent to enable deployers to interpret a system’s output and use it appropriately.
@ref Art 13(1) first sentence (src:332)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way as to ensure that its operation is sufficiently transparent to enable deployers to interpret a system's output and use it appropriately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) first sentence the high-risk AI system is designed and developed so that its operation is sufficiently transparent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 13, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the high-risk AI system is designed and developed in such a way as to ensure that its operation is sufficiently transparent to enable deployers to interpret a system's output and use it appropriately`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed in such a way as to ensure that their operation is sufficiently transparent to enable deployers to interpret a system's output and use it appropriately"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:332 | An appropriate type and degree of transparency shall be ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3.
@ref Art 13(1) second sentence (src:332)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) second sentence an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to compliance with the obligations of the provider and deployer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 13, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`an appropriate type and degree of transparency is ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appropriate type and degree of transparency shall be ensured with a view to achieving compliance with the relevant obligations of the provider and deployer set out in Section 3"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 13(2): instructions for use`

-- src:333 | 2. High-risk AI systems shall be accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise that include concise, complete, correct and clear information that is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers.
@ref Art 13(2) (src:333)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use include concise, complete, correct and clear information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use that include concise, complete, correct and clear information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 13, "", 2)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the high-risk AI system is accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise` AND `the instructions for use include concise, complete, correct and clear information` AND `the information is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "High-risk AI systems shall be accompanied by instructions for use in an appropriate digital format or otherwise that include concise, complete, correct and clear information that is relevant, accessible and comprehensible to deployers"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Article 13(3): what the instructions for use contain`

-- src:334 | 3. The instructions for use shall contain at least the following information:
-- src:335 | (a) the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where applicable, of its authorised representative;
-- src:336 | (b) the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system, including:
-- src:337 | (i) its intended purpose;
-- src:338 | (ii) the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity;
-- src:339 | (iii) any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2);
-- src:340 | (iv) where applicable, the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output;
-- src:341 | (v) when appropriate, its performance regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used;
-- src:342 | (vi) when appropriate, specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system;
-- src:343 | (vii) where applicable, information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately;
-- src:344 | (c) the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if any;
-- src:345 | (d) the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers;
-- src:346 | (e) the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates;
-- src:347 | (f) where relevant, a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allows deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12.
@ref Art 13(3) (src:334-347)
-- "at least": the list gives the minimum; each listed item is needed (a missing one is the text's own no). The qualifiers of items (a), (b)(iv), (v), (vi), (vii), (c) and (f) are folded into each item's yes or no (fork F-qualifier-fold).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the instructions for use contain the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where applicable, of its authorised representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain its intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain where applicable, the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, its performance regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain where applicable, information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instructions for use contain where relevant, a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allows deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) the instructions for use contain at least the following information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 13, "", 3)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the instructions for use contain the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where applicable, of its authorised representative` AND `the instructions for use contain the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system` AND `the instructions for use contain its intended purpose` AND `the instructions for use contain the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity` AND `the instructions for use contain any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2)` AND `the instructions for use contain where applicable, the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output` AND `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, its performance regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used` AND `the instructions for use contain when appropriate, specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system` AND `the instructions for use contain where applicable, information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately` AND `the instructions for use contain the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if any` AND `the instructions for use contain the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers` AND `the instructions for use contain the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates` AND `the instructions for use contain where relevant, a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allows deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The instructions for use shall contain at least the following information:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed
